<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Orseolo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1010–after 1046</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Peter of Hungary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Orseolo was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1038 to 1041 and again from 1044 to 1046. The son of a Venetian doge and a sister of Stephen I, he was named Stephen's heir but was soon deposed in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-aba">Samuel Aba</a>. Restored by Emperor Henry III after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-menfo">Battle of Ménfő</a>, he did homage for his kingdom, but he was overthrown and blinded in the pagan uprising of 1046.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-orseolo.jpg" alt="Peter Orseolo" width="320" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Márk Kálti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%A9pes_kr%C3%B3nika_-_47.oldal_-_P%C3%A9ter_kir%C3%A1ly.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
